layout: _layouts/base.njk
section: tools
description: Client-side cipher toolkit from sp3ctr-zone. Nothing typed here leaves your browser.
extraScripts:
  - /js/tools.js
---
<h1>tools</h1>
<p class="prompt">client-side only. nothing you type below leaves your
  browser — there's no server to send it to. view-source and verify
  that yourself, that's the point.</p>
<p class="prompt">the moment a tool needs a server, it needs your trust
  too — and servers get subpoenaed, sold, or breached. anything that
  actually has to stay yours belongs on your own machine, not in someone
  else's database.</p>

<section class="panel">
  <h2>cipher toolkit</h2>

  <form id="cipher-form">
    <div class="row">
      <div class="field">
        <label for="cipher-type">cipher</label>
        <select id="cipher-type">
          <option value="caesar">caesar shift</option>
          <option value="vigenere">vigenère</option>
          <option value="xor">xor (hex output)</option>
        </select>
      </div>
      <div class="field">
        <label for="cipher-key"><span id="cipher-key-label">shift</span></label>
        <input id="cipher-key" type="text" autocomplete="off" placeholder="e.g. 13">
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="field">
      <label for="cipher-message">message</label>
      <textarea id="cipher-message" placeholder="type or paste here"></textarea>
    </div>

    <div class="actions">
      <button type="submit" value="encrypt">encrypt</button>
      <button type="submit" value="decrypt">decrypt</button>
    </div>

    <div class="field">
      <label for="cipher-output">output</label>
      <textarea id="cipher-output" readonly></textarea>
    </div>
    <div class="actions">
      <button type="button" id="cipher-copy">copy output</button>
    </div>
  </form>

  <p class="note">these are classic ciphers, kept around for learning and
    for the vibe — not for real secrecy. a determined adversary breaks
    caesar and vigenère by hand and xor with a short reused key almost
    as fast. for anything that actually needs to stay secret, reach for
    PGP, age, or Signal instead.</p>
</section>
